Package: emozi
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: fonts-noto-color-emoji, at-spi2-core
Description: macOS-style emoji picker for Linux desktops
 Emozi opens a small, native-looking emoji picker when you press Super+.
 Start typing to search by name, keyword or :shortcode:, then press Enter
 to type the emoji straight into the application you were using.
 .
 Features:
  - all Unicode 17.0 emoji, filtered to what your fonts can display
  - opens next to the text cursor (via AT-SPI) or at the mouse pointer
  - frequently used emoji and per-emoji skin-tone memory
  - follows the GTK theme, light or dark
  - configurable shortcut, registered with Cinnamon's keyboard settings
